&#8220;I&#8217;m genuinely trying to find the words to help explain what&#8217;s going on in my brain today,&#8221; she began. &#8220;Thank you so much for loving this song, for listening to it&#8230; I&#8217;m running out of hyperboles to describe how I feel.&#8221;

Langley continued: &#8220;Just thank you so much, it&#8217;s changing my life, it&#8217;s changing the lives of the writers of this song. It&#8217;s changing the lives of my family and it is truly growing an atmosphere for something I&#8217;m gonna be able to do the rest of my life.&#8221;

The 27-year-old singer explained that she planned to take a break and enjoy the night celebrating with her team.

&#8220;Today doesn&#8217;t feel like a real thing,&#8221; she added. &#8220;It feels fake and somebody&#8217;s gonna be like, &#8216;Ha ha, we&#8217;re kidding the whole time.&#8217; I&#8217;m gonna go out and celebrate tonight. I&#8217;m really excited to just experience a moment like this in my life. Just thank you so much.&#8221;

Langley wrote in the caption: &#8220;23 weeks Texas forever.&#8221; Before reflecting in a video from her backyard on IG, she reacted briefly with a post to her IG Story hours earlier Tuesday, calling the achievement &#8220;absolutely insane.&#8221;

&#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8221; debuted in the top 40 of the Hot 100 at No. 39 in November and surged to spend 23 non-consecutive weeks at No. 1, which dethroned Mariah Carey’s “All I Want for Christmas” as the record-holder.

The Ella Langley train doesn&#8217;t appear to be slowing down either: She&#8217;ll return to the stage on her Dandelion Tour in Knoxville, Tennessee, on Thursday.

